  "paragraphs": [
    "partition_code: 113 of 119 rows have known values (95.0% coverage).",
    "At k = 20, mean shared-label agreement is 100.0% when weighting positive anchor\u2013label pairs, and 100.0% when weighting labels equally. Mean individual label lift is 3 and equal-label lift is 3.03. Mean lift is not aggregate purity divided by aggregate chance.",
    "1 \u00b7 Segment A: 43 known positives; 43 evaluable positive anchors have 100.0% mean agreement, versus 38.1% reference prevalence (lift 2.628). An average of 18.91 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "2 \u00b7 Segment C: 36 known positives; 36 evaluable positive anchors have 100.0% mean agreement, versus 31.9% reference prevalence (lift 3.139). An average of 18.22 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "0 \u00b7 Segment A: 34 known positives; 34 evaluable positive anchors have 100.0% mean agreement, versus 30.1% reference prevalence (lift 3.324). An average of 19.56 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "Known-neighbor coverage at this k is 94.4%. Unknown neighbors are excluded from agreement denominators; missing annotations can bias the result.",
    "The saved null comparison gives an empirical one-sided p-value of 0.25 for macro_lift. This tests the specified shuffle, not semantic understanding; use the combined multiple-testing table and practical effect sizes when judging the finding.",
    "The probe panel measures recoverability on a held-out split. Compare each model with its baseline; recoverability and nearest-neighbor usefulness answer different questions.",
    "baseline: balanced_accuracy 0.3333, macro_f1 0.1802; 27 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
    "linear: balanced_accuracy 1, macro_f1 1; 27 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
    "Embedding A normalization comparison on identical held-out rows: raw_standardized: balanced_accuracy 1, unit: balanced_accuracy 1, unit_standardized: balanced_accuracy 1, norm_only: balanced_accuracy 0.1833. Direction-only and magnitude-only scores describe accessible information for these pipelines; fit telemetry does not establish encoder-training stability.",
    "In the raw_euclidean filtration for embedding A, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 2 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "In the unit_chordal filtration for embedding A, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 2 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "Next: compare feature measurements across scales, check probe gains against baselines, or summarize a selected region. Shared labels and correlated features can suggest patterns, but do not establish why the model retrieved an item."
